Resizable sidebar, translucent panels, boxed surfaces
====================================================

Three requests, and only one of them was ever CSS.

1. Resize. The sidebar was a hard 228px grid column. It is now `var(--sidebar-width, 228px)` with a
   6px drag strip on its edge, and the width is stored as a backend preference like the theme — the
   installation's, not one window's. Arrow keys nudge it (shift for a bigger step) so it does not
   depend on a steady hand.

2. Boxes. Everything that holds content — composer, suggestion cards, panels, settings panes — gets a
   real border, a 14px radius and a 1px accent-tinted inner highlight, so the page has structure
   instead of text floating on a black field. The composer border lights up on focus.

3. Translucency. `.sidebar` and the panels become `color-mix()` over transparent with a
   backdrop blur, wrapped in `@supports`, so on a compositor without backdrop-filter the same colours
   are simply opaque and nothing breaks. Window-level transparency is the compositor's business and is
   NOT done here — a KWin rule does that.

Both surface options are switches in Settings, General, and are stored as preferences rather than
being hardcoded: "Boxed surfaces" and "Translucent panels".

